<title>PAKISTAN: Shell Pakistan up 5.0 percent.</title>
<headline>Shell Pakistan up 5.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Pakistan rose 10 rupees, or 5.0 percent, to 210 rupees on Wednesday after the firm announced a 35 percent interim dividend, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shell, which announced its first half results on Tuesday, also said it recorded an after-tax profit of 379 million rupees for the half year ended December 31, 1996, against 102 million rupees in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Turnover of 13,000 shares of the blue chip had been recorded at the Karachi bourse by noon.</p>
<p>&quot;Shell, along with the other oil marketing companies has performed well,&quot; dealer Shakeel Anwar said.</p>
<p>Shell has an 18.5 percent share in Pakistan's oil products distribution market worth an estimated 100 billion rupees a year. It is 51 percent owned by Royal Dutch Petroleum Co.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
